  "term": "nearsightedness",
  "definition": "Nearsightedness is a focusing problem of the eye where incoming light comes to a point before it reaches the retina when the eye is not adjusting focus. It is associated with a cornea that bends light too much or an eyeball that is longer than usual from front to back.",
